te remote match; tryCommit selects voting-member quorum match and asks the log to commit only in the current term. Followers validate the preceding log term, append, and bound advertised commit by the matched suffix. Initial A2 trace: elections reset term/votes/progress and gather votes after log freshness checks; higher-term dispatch changes role and lower-term messages are dropped. Reset discards pending read confirmations and initializes follower progress, while leader promotion appends a current-term no-op. Election is suppressed when committed work has not yet applied, with a comment explicitly tying this to membership/quorum safety. These traces do not yet establish persistence ordering or application/membership completion. Early sourced discrepancy: readIndex.confirm releases a prefix of pending requests and retains each request ctx/from, but handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation sends every remote response using the confirming message Hint/HintHigh, whereas local completion uses s.ctx. Followers copy the response context to ReadyToRead; pendingReadIndex.addReady selects a batch by exact SystemCtx. Thus a prefix request with a different context appears not to receive its own completion key. Timeout/GC exists and is contrary evidence against permanent resource retention; no execution or normative conclusion is claimed.\",\n        \"remaining\": [\n          \"Complete the A1/A2 backbone through peer update, persistence/message ordering, application, membership changes, recovery and public completion contracts before registering a focused Candidate.\",\n          \"Determine whether ordinary request batching and transport ordering permit two distinct forwarded read contexts to be queued before the later context is confirmed, and whether any other response/retry path restores the earlier context.\",\n          \"Inspect membership eligibility at read-confirmation admission, since the leader wrapper also accepts observers; do not assume that every accepted heartbeat