{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The captured transport can drop a message when its send queue is full, and NodeHost does not retry a failed send itself. That permits a simple history: drop the first read’s confirmation heartbeats, then deliver the second read’s heartbeats in order. An existing test also expects prefix release to preserve each request’s context. I’ll frame the obligation around that identity-preservation duty, without asserting a client completion deadline.\n"}}
