requests covered by a later confirmation. The confirming request context must not replace an earlier released request identity.',source_ids=ids,scope=dict(description='ReadIndex prefix release and remote result identity in a stable leader term and unchanged voting membership after a current-term entry has committed.',assumptions=['Crash-free execution with valid known peers and non-Byzantine messages produced by those peers','Distinct nonzero-low contexts for concurrently pending requests','Message loss is permitted; surviving messages retain their per-route order','Peer caller processes and persists updates before sending ordinary messages'],excluded=['No numeric completion bound, eventual successful client completion, or permanent resource-retention proposition','No whole-cluster linearizability violation asserted','No membership change, restart, Byzantine traffic, context collision, storage fault or snapshot during the observed read suffix']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=ids,expectation_ids=['src-read-prefix-expectation'],binding_ids=['bind-read-publish','bind-read-consume'],derivation='The prefix test independently specifies that earlier released statuses retain their own ctx/from. Peer.ReadIndex accepts the supplied SystemCtx as request identity, and the public interface promises an outcome for the returned request. The actual requester consumes readiness by exact SystemCtx; no index-only association or prefix-completion API exists there. Consequently remote publication of a released status must carry that status identity to its requester. This is a local correlation duty, not an inference that every admitted read must succeed before its timeout. The release handler is implementation evidence and the suspected deviation, not normative authority by itself.',applicability='Only confirmed prefix members in the same leader readIndex lifetime are covered. Transport loss before confirmation does not excuse misidentification after the implementation elects to release a request.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Local publication already uses s.ctx; the remote branch may nevertheless differ','Timeout satisfies a later failure outcome but does not repair correlation of a released successful read status']))\nbindings=[dict(id='bind-read-publish',material_id='src-read-confirm-send',symbol='handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation',start_line=1771,end_line=1790,description='Consumes released read statuses and creates local or remote completion publications.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claimid,source_ids=ids,rationale='This is the exact remote publication boundary required to preserve the released request identity.')]),dict(id='bind-read-consume',material_id='src-read-consume',symbol='addReady',start_line=861,end_line=873,description='Matches published readiness to requester batch by exact complete SystemCtx.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claimid,source_ids=['src-read-consume','src-api-read'],rationale='A substituted context cannot complete the original pending batch at this consumer.')])]\ns=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=cid,question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=bindings,sources=new,rationale='Contract/test investigation grounds a local read-result identity obligation. Transport admission failure permits loss of initial confirmation heartbeats followed by in-order delivery of later work, so a controlled schedule need not invent reordered replies.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[cid,'B-read-forward','B-read-confirm','src-transport-loss','src-nodehost-send','src-read-prefix-expectation'],answered='Transport.send returns false on channel-full/rate-limit admission; NodeHost.sendMessage ignores the ordinary Send return. Dropping an initial read heartbeat and delivering a later heartbeat therefore fits the captured failure boundary without changing per-route ordering. readindex_test explicitly asserts original ctx/from for each prefix member. Together with exact-context consumer lookup this grounds publication identity preservation independently of any deadline. The next artifact can use real Peer constructors and generated messages, persist each Update to the existing TestLogDB, and compare original contexts with responses after prefix release.',remaining=['Construct and execute the fixed Peer-level controlled schedule; inspect actual identities, prefix release and follower readiness.','Full NodeHost timeout and application endpoint consequences are outside this local proposition.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The missing legal-history and local responsibility premises now have captured sources; execution remains necessary to measure the candidate discrepancy.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_19-33-36-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
